WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:06.120
The Sanderson Sisters are back for a nostalgic,&nbsp;
fun-filled sequel, stacked with easter eggs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.680
deep-cut references to the original movie.
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, I'm Jan and I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.520
been re-watching and pausing Hocus&nbsp;
Pocus 2 to uncover all the amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:19.140
little details you might have missed!
The movie begins with a wicked flashback to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:24.960
Salem 1653 and Winifred's sixteenth birthday.
And the creepy spider that young Sarah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.200
gifts to Winnie…
You will love it!
&nbsp;

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.720
…is a sly reference to Sarah's love&nbsp;
of spiders in the original movie.
&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.360
What a pretty spider!
The costume department&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.520
also honoured Sarah's affection for the creepy&nbsp;
crawlies on her new costume, which has sleeves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.020
made to look like crocheted spider webs.
And if you look really closely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:47.820
you'll spot some spiders embroidered among&nbsp;
the floral and thorn design on her bodice.
&nbsp;

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:53.580
After fleeing the Salem mob into the Forbidden&nbsp;
Woods, the three young sisters form a calming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
circle and amusingly think about the Reverend&nbsp;
screaming and other deliciously terrible things.
&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.760
Think soothing thoughts.
The smell of fresh mud.
&nbsp;

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:08.340
The Reverend's scream when he saw the spider.
This moment calls back to how the adult Sandersons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.780
form a circle when they're stressed out in&nbsp;
the first movie and the hilariously awful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:13.680
things they think about.
Think soothing thoughts.
&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.020
Rabid bats
Black death.
&nbsp;

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:20.040
Mummy's scorpion pie.
The "Come Little Children" tune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:23.640
that the young Sisters hear in the woods&nbsp;
is the same one in the original film.
&nbsp;

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.800
And notice how it's young Sarah who becomes&nbsp;
entranced by the song, reflecting the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.360
that she's the one who will sing it to lure&nbsp;
the children of Salem over 400 years later.
&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.100
Now, pay close attention to the Witch&nbsp;
Mother and her costume in this scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.780
as the embroidered eye on her outfit&nbsp;
reappears many times throughout the movie.
&nbsp;

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.740
It's a reference to the eye on the&nbsp;
spell-book that she gifts to Winnie.
&nbsp;

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:52.020
And Winifred also has eyes embroidered on&nbsp;
her costume when she returns later on.
&nbsp;

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.180
The broach around the Witch Mother's neck is&nbsp;
also identical to the one used as Winnie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:01.200
belt buckle, and the stones match the&nbsp;
colour of each of their outfits.
&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.240
Moving on to present-day Salem, and the name&nbsp;
of the school Becca, Izzy and Cassie go to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.340
is Samuel Skelton, the name of a real-life&nbsp;
Puritan who settled in Salem and founded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.300
the First Church in the town.
And notice when Izzy arrives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.220
the scarf she's wearing is covered in eyes,&nbsp;
another creepy little reference to Book.
&nbsp;

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:24.780
While Becca is waiting outside the&nbsp;
principal's office, the assistant may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:29.820
be wearing a ladybird outfit, but these look&nbsp;
a lot like Mickey or Minnie Mouse hands.
&nbsp;

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:34.380
In the sequel, we discover the Sanderson&nbsp;
Sisters' old home has been converted into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.460
Gilbert's Old Salem Magic Shoppe.
And the cauldron of cats filled with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:43.740
stuffed toy black cats is likely a nod to&nbsp;
Thackery Binx who knocked over the witches'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:48.180
cauldron of potion in the first movie&nbsp;
and was transformed into a black cat.
&nbsp;

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:52.020
There's also a ton of Sanderson&nbsp;
Sisters merchandise in the shop,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:57.120
including these doll versions of them here.
When Gilbert reveals the Book of Spells to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.520
audience at the shop, pause and look really&nbsp;
closely at the straps holding Book down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:07.920
in particular the little grill over the eye, which&nbsp;
is a deliberate homage to Hannibal Lecter's mouth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.180
restraint in Silence of the Lambs.
And the costume Gilbert wears during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:16.380
his presentation has eyes on both the&nbsp;
hat and the cloak, referencing book.
&nbsp;

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.440
Plus, there are eyes on the&nbsp;
door he emerges through here.
&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.360
After Becca and Izzy arrive at the shop,&nbsp;
you'll need to pause really quickly here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.860
to spot the Houdini poster on the wall&nbsp;
when Cobweb appears out of nowhere.
&nbsp;

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:34.200
The question "Do spirits return?" is some&nbsp;
sneaky foreshadowing for how Becca and Izzy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:39.060
who are also in this shot, will accidentally bring&nbsp;
the Sanderson Sisters back to life later on.
&nbsp;

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:44.760
It's an awesome moment when the sisters finally&nbsp;
return with Winnie slapping both Sarah and Mary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:49.348
in the stomach, in a deliberate hat-tip to how&nbsp;
she gut-punched Sarah in the original movie.
&nbsp;

00:03:49.348 --> 00:03:53.340
Amok, amok, amok, amok, amok...
The song they sing here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.660
"The Witches Are Back", is an amusing take&nbsp;
on Elton John's "The Bitch Is Back".
&nbsp;

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:01.800
After the trio catch Becca and&nbsp;
Izzy, the girls play a trick on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.180
them by pretending they're witches too.
We only look young, but really, we're 40.
&nbsp;

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.315
Oh, 40?
Old folks, huh?
&nbsp;

00:04:07.315 --> 00:04:11.640
Very fine physician.
This reminds me of the ruse Max plays to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:15.660
escape the witches in the original movie.
You've messed with the great and powerful Max.
&nbsp;

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.885
I summon the Burning Rain of Death!
The Burning Rain of Death?
&nbsp;

00:04:18.885 --> 00:04:20.509
Burning Rain of Death?
I don't know.
&nbsp;

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:23.100
(ALL GASPING)
The hilarious supermarket scene in the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:27.840
film, where the Sanderson Sisters gulp down&nbsp;
beauty creams and lotions in the misguided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.760
belief they contain the souls of deceased&nbsp;
children, is a deep-cut reference to a deleted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.126
scene from the first movie.
Delicious!
&nbsp;

00:04:35.126 --> 00:04:38.340
Floral, but with a woodsy finish.
Tis tingly.
&nbsp;

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:42.300
My favourite feeling.
So far, the full deleted scene hasn't been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:48.480
released but one of the original trailers for the&nbsp;
1993 movie does show Mary downing various liquids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:53.700
in a supermarket and looking to eat a child.
 
And the sisters' funny walk they do as they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:58.200
explore the store is a call-back to the walk&nbsp;
they did after they came back to life in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:58.740
first movie.
Get him.
&nbsp;

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:06.060
Becca, Izzy and Cassie also pay homage to the&nbsp;
walk at the end of the movie when they suddenly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:11.580
find themselves doing it without realizing it.
When Becca and Izzy use salt to protect themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:16.200
from the sisters' dark magic, it's a nod to&nbsp;
how Allison used salt in the first movie.
&nbsp;

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:21.506
And given Becca turns out to be a witch in&nbsp;
the sequel and Winnie remarked about Allison…
&nbsp;

00:05:21.506 --> 00:05:25.860
What a clever little white witch.
…it adds to the popular fan theory that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:31.620
Allison was a secret witch herself all along.
The brooms the sisters fly off on in the sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:37.860
get a fun update to modern cleaning and vacuum&nbsp;
tech in 2022, compared to the 1993 movie.
&nbsp;

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:44.160
Sarah gets an upgraded mop and Mary finds a&nbsp;
pair of robot vacuums, which also play a crucial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:48.900
role later on when they break the salt circle&nbsp;
keeping them trapped at the Traske household.
&nbsp;

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:55.260
Now, if you're wondering why Mary says "Cowabunga"&nbsp;
as she flies off, it's a wink to Kathy Najimy's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.260 --> 00:06:00.300
role as Mayor of Witch Town in the Rise of&nbsp;
the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles show.
&nbsp;

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:05.340
And as the three hatch their plan which&nbsp;
ends up being suspiciously similar to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.780
one in the first movie, Sarah responds to&nbsp;
Winnie with a line from the original film.
&nbsp;

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:10.063
Then we run amok in Salem!
Amok!
&nbsp;

00:06:10.063 --> 00:06:13.404
Amok, amok, amok, amok, amok...
Stop that!
&nbsp;

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:18.780
The first step in their scheme is to return to&nbsp;
their old cottage, and the way the door swings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:23.220
open amid flashes of light is a tribute to the&nbsp;
same way they returned in the first movie.
&nbsp;

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.760
This time though, Sarah is disappointed&nbsp;
at the state of the place…
&nbsp;

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:31.260
Where are all the cobwebs...
and my rat tails?
&nbsp;

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:35.820
This is an amusing nod to the first thing&nbsp;
she did in the OG movie after arriving back.
&nbsp;

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:38.820
My lucky rat tail!
And the way she goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:43.620
searching for her rat tails by hanging from the&nbsp;
rafters is a throwback to when she swung from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:48.660
the cemetery gates in the original movie.
Sarah's response to Gilbert revealing himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.400
to the trio…
A boy.
&nbsp;

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:54.900
…is a shout-out to the three sister's&nbsp;
reaction when they first saw Thackery Binx.
&nbsp;

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.640
(GASPING)
A boy!
&nbsp;

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.080
…as well as to Sarah's generally&nbsp;
boy-crazy ways back in the 90s.
&nbsp;

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:05.040
Boys will love me!
When Gilbert tells the sisters he saw them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:11.220
on Halloween night in 1993, he mentions "a bunch&nbsp;
of boys stole his candy", referencing the bullies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:15.840
Jay and Ice, who harassed Max and Dani for&nbsp;
their Halloween candy in the original movie.
&nbsp;

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:21.060
And the empty cloth container Gilbert used&nbsp;
for his candy also looks like it's probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:26.520
this Mickey and Minnie Mouse pillowcase.
There's some pun-tastic stall names at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:32.520
Scare Fest, such as Apple Plectic, which is a&nbsp;
play on the word apoplectic, and a stall where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:36.180
participants have to bob for apples.
They're drowning a man.
&nbsp;

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:39.120
How charming.
There's also Lifestyles of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:45.180
Witch and Famous, a nod to the 80s and 90s reality&nbsp;
TV series "Lifestyles of the Rich and Famous".
&nbsp;

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:50.220
And there's a "Bone Appetit And Grave&nbsp;
E" food stall with a wicked witch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:54.480
selling poisoned apples strolling by,&nbsp;
a reference to Disney's Snow White.
&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:08:00.060
And while mayor Traske is waiting in line for&nbsp;
his caramel apple, there's a man behind him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:04.140
dressed like the devil and a woman wearing&nbsp;
a dressing gown and rollers in her hair.
&nbsp;

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:08.280
These are a sly reference to the scene from&nbsp;
the first movie when the sisters thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:12.780
they were meeting their master, Satan&nbsp;
himself, and also met his wife who was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:14.160
getting ready for bed at the time.
Sisters, Satan has married Medusa.
&nbsp;

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.540
See the snakes in her hair?
And the scene with that couple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:22.260
from the first film actually appears&nbsp;
when Winnie stumbles across another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:27.780
couple watching the original Hocus Pocus movie.
The fact the events of the first film exist as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:32.040
movie in this universe shows just how famous&nbsp;
the Sanderson Sisters are in that world.
&nbsp;

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:37.200
Just like the first movie, the Sisters sing a&nbsp;
song at the Halloween festival in the sequel.
&nbsp;

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.360
I bet you're looking for the stage.
Always.
&nbsp;

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:44.100
And if you pause here, there's some nice&nbsp;
details for the various other acts like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:49.380
"The Broom Brigade", "The Acro Bats",&nbsp;
and "Hades Hotties" which is a reference&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:54.060
to the Greek god of the underworld, who's the&nbsp;
villain in the 1990s Disney movie Hercules.
&nbsp;

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:59.640
When the sisters put a spell on the Scare Fest&nbsp;
audience, and have them dance down the street,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.600
there's a definite vibe of the music&nbsp;
video for Michael Jackson's Thriller.
&nbsp;

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:08.760
There's also some great easter eggs in the&nbsp;
crowd, such as this lady with a Madonna outfit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:12.960
a reference to the costume worn by Max&nbsp;
and Dani's mum on Halloween night.
&nbsp;

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:18.120
And it also looks like someone's wearing the&nbsp;
Sorcerer Mickey Mouse hat from Fantasia.
&nbsp;

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:23.340
After the sisters discover Becca&nbsp;
hiding, Winnie can't remember her name…
&nbsp;

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:23.986
What's her name again?
Uh...
&nbsp;

00:09:23.986 --> 00:09:26.760
Shishka-baby?
…which is the same thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:31.200
Mary calls Dani when she finds her in the first&nbsp;
movie, which is a pun on the food shish-kebab.
&nbsp;

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:35.700
Shish kebaby!
As Traske arrives back home to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:41.100
the sisters trapped in his garage, he gets out&nbsp;
of his car and Winnie calls it a very small bus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:45.900
an amusing reference to their first encounter&nbsp;
with motorised transport in the first movie.
&nbsp;

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:48.600
What is this contraption?
I call it a bus.
&nbsp;

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:54.240
When Sarah and Mary fade into dust as the price&nbsp;
Winnie pays for the Magicae Maxima spell, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:59.040
say goodbye in the same way they bade farewell&nbsp;
after the sun came up in the first movie.
&nbsp;

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:01.569
Bye-bye.
Goodbye.
&nbsp;

00:10:01.569 --> 00:10:04.380
Bye-bye.
Goodbye.
&nbsp;

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:08.700
Although Billy says the final destruction&nbsp;
of the sisters is what has now released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:13.440
him from the curses placed on him by Winnie,
if you watch to the very end of the credits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:19.020
there's a bonus scene where Cobweb reveals that&nbsp;
Gilbert has a second Black Flame candle in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:23.940
possession, which means we could easily see the&nbsp;
Sanderson Sisters return again for a third movie.
&nbsp;

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:27.360
Let me know what you think about&nbsp;
that and any other comments below.
